WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.167
-Welcome back.

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:05.801
I'm hanging out with Colson
Baker, a.k.a. Machine Gun Kelly.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:07.501
His new movie, "Good Mourning,"

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:09.567
is in theaters
and on demand now.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.334
And his album
"Mainstream Sellout"

00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:12.667
is also out now.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.701
Colson, I wanted to try
something fun with you.

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:17.801
I thought we could act out
a dramatic scene together, okay?

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:19.534
But first we have to
fill in the blanks.

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.334
It is time for
"Mad Lib Theater."

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:22.334
Here we go.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.334
♪ Mad Lib Theater ♪

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:26.934
♪ Ah-ah, yeah! ♪

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.434
-Alright.
So here's how this works.

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:31.067
I'm gonna ask you for some
silly words -- nouns, verbs,

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:33.567
adjectives, et cetera --
and they'll all be written

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:35.434
onto our cue cards here,
as we're doing this.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.634
And then we're gonna act out
a dramatic Mad Libs scene.

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.067
Are you ready for this?

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:40.467
-Thank God
I went to the fourth grade.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:42.300
-Okay. Here we go.
I want a noun --

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.501
-Nouns, adjectives...

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:46.868
-Yes. I want a noun
that begins with a C.

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:48.000
-Koala.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.734
Uh -- Uh, wait. Computer.

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:54.033
-Computer. Good.
Computer's good.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.701
Adjective.

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:57.968
-Stinky.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:00:59.734
-Type of bug.

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:01.467
-Caterpillar.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:03.601
-Animal.
-Koala. Koala!

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:05.100
-Koala. Okay, good. Yeah.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.167
[ Applause ]

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:10.100
They got your back.
They got your back.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.133
A chain restaurant.

00:01:12.133 --> 00:01:13.667
-Chipotle. I used to work there.

00:01:13.667 --> 00:01:14.968
-Chipotle?
-Yeah.

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:17.300
-Noun.
-Baby.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:21.767
-Okay. Baby. Okay.
-Baby.

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:24.300
-A kitchen appliance.
-Spatula.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:28.634
-I love that you're --
you're so confident on spatula.

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:30.701
That was the one, you're like,
"Oh, no, no, yeah.

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:33.033
Spatula, of course."

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:35.300
A plural noun.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.334
-Fungi.

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:39.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.367
Right?
-Wow. That's next-level.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.968
That's next --
That's next-level.

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:45.300
Fungi.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.100
Another animal.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.234
-Platypus.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.701
-Platypus.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:52.234
One of the Seven Dwarves.

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:54.300
-Oh, I never watched that movie.
-Sleepy!

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.300
-Smokey. What?
-Smokey.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.934
-Uh, what?
-Smokey.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:00.200
-Sleepy. Sleepy.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.467
-No, no, I'm writing
down Smokey because --

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:04.934
Celebrity name.

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:06.200
[ Audience shouting ]

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:08.033
-Benedict Cumberbatch.

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:10.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:13.334
-Benedict Cumberbatch.

00:02:13.334 --> 00:02:14.667
Name me a number.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.167
-Just eleven -- eleven --
-Eleven tousand.

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:17.701
-Tousand, with a T-O-U.

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:18.667
Eleven tousand.

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.100
-Eleven tousand.
-Yes.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.601
-Type of profession.

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:22.868
-Genie.

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:25.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.467
-Wow! Speed round. Here we go.

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:30.067
Another plural noun.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:32.534
-Moose.
-Moose. Mooses?

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:33.934
What?

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:36.167
-Moose. What is going on?

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:41.133
Uh, okay. Body part.
Watch it.

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:44.434
-Yeah. Elbow.
-Elbow!

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:46.601
-What?
-Wow. That was weird.

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:49.434
Phrase that you would say
if you bumped

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:51.801
into Leonardo DiCaprio
on the street.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.133
[ Audience shouting ]

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.334
[ Fingers snapping ]

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:56.000
-"You --
Why did you let go, Jack?

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.734
You should have
stayed on the door.

00:02:57.734 --> 00:02:59.534
You should've got on the door."

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:01.067
"Why did you let go, Jack?

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:02.601
There was room
for you on the door."

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:04.901
-Alright.
"Why did you let go, Jack?"

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:07.067
Another noun.

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:08.567
-You do this one.

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:11.400
-Burrito.
-Burrito.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.734
-Type of drink.

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:15.801
-Bloody Mary.
-Bloody Mary.

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:17.701
Another celebrity.

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:19.200
-Waka Flocka Flame.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.300
-Flocka Flame.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.267
Verb ending in I-N-G.

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.801
-Clenching.
-Clenching?

00:03:28.801 --> 00:03:32.868
-I'm -- I'm sorry.
I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

00:03:32.868 --> 00:03:35.601
-This is fun doing Mad Libs
with you.

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:39.200
What you'd shout if you sat down
in a seat that's wet.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.267
-"Aah."

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:42.634
-A high pitched "aah"?

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:44.167
-"Aah."
-"Aah."

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:46.200
First concert you ever attended.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.267
-Oh. Backstreet Boys. What's up?

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:52.534
-Wow. Backstreet boys.

00:03:52.534 --> 00:03:53.901
A professional athlete.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:55.968
-Tiger Woods!
-Tom Brady.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:59.000
-Alright. Tom Brady. Tom Brady.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.033
Another verb ending in I-N-G.

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:02.434
-Crying.
-Crying.

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:04.801
Yes, good. Crying.

00:04:04.801 --> 00:04:07.701
Two words that rhyme.

00:04:07.701 --> 00:04:10.868
-Garage, Minaj.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:14.767
-Wow. Garage, Minaj.

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:17.601
A long, silly word.

00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:20.100
-Iridocyclitis!

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.634
-What?!

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:24.200
-Is that a disease?
-Is that an actual --

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.200
Yeah. What is that?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.501
-"Iri-dopta--dacly--"

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:29.734
I'm happy the edibles
are kicking in.

00:04:29.734 --> 00:04:31.968
This is a...

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:35.133
-"Iridocyclitis."
-Yeah, we --

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.667
-Iridocyclitis. Yeah, of course.

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:39.100
Alright, now, we've filled out
the words for our scene.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.868
Good luck to our cue card.

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:44.067
So sorry, Roman.

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.234
Are you ready
to perform our scene?

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:49.667
-I don't know now.
-Let's go. Let's do this.

00:04:49.667 --> 00:04:51.067
-Okay.
-Here we go.

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:52.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:55.467
